{
 "name": "table-size",
 "what": "the size of one small program for 32-bit ARM, in bytes: .text, .rodata and their sum, at five states of the headers and in four forms",
 "purpose_in_the_task_list": "Owner, 2026-11-14: the half word table (128 words for the bytes under 0x80, the byte itself from 0x80 on) is measured before the choice between it and the word tables of 256 entries. This run gives the size of the program with the half tables beside the states of the run table-size-20261114T091231Z.json; the time of the half tables is in the run scalar-writers-20261114T093713Z.json",
 "method": "one build of each state and form, no repetition; the size of each section is read with arm-linux-gnueabihf-size -A from the linked program; a size has no noise, so no round, median or spread is given; the size of each escape table that the linked program holds is read with arm-linux-gnueabihf-nm -S (nm of the host binutils reads the same files)",
 "states": {"4dac08e": "before the tables (before commit 5 of plan A4)", "f331cd1": "the five tables of 256 words of 8 bytes (the head of claude/escape-room-a before this run)", "f331cd1+class-tables": "f331cd1 with bench/probes/table-size/class-tables.patch applied to the exported escape.hpp: the class form of arm 4 of the probe scalar-writers, a table of 256 classes of one byte and a table of the words of the classes for each context", "f331cd1+class-fields": "f331cd1 with bench/probes/table-size/class-fields.patch: the class form of arm 5, the classes of the five contexts in bit fields of one table of 256 entries of 16 bits", "f331cd1+half-tables": "f331cd1 with bench/probes/table-size/half-tables.patch: the five tables of 128 words for the bytes under 0x80 and the byte itself for a byte from 0x80 on, the form of arm 7 of the probe scalar-writers; the html table kEntities stays at 256 words"},
 "forms": {"none": "compile(source) with no media type", "html": "compile(source, \"text/html\")", "json": "compile(source, \"application/json\")", "runtime": "compile(source, media type read through a volatile pointer, \"application/json\")"},
 "program": "bench/probes/table-size/probe.cpp: compiles one template of three tags, renders it over a std::map<std::string, std::string> and writes the answer with std::puts",
 "builds": "arm-linux-gnueabihf-g++-16 -std=c++23 -Os -mthumb -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -Wall -Wextra -Werror, linked with -Wl,--gc-sections against the shared libstdc++, libgcc_s and libc; target armv7-a+fp, hard float (the defaults of the compiler)",
 "headers": "include/ of each state, exported with git archive; for a state <commit>+<name>, run.sh applies <name>.patch of the probe directory with patch -p1. In the exported copy of 4dac08e the script gives the lambda indent_at of compile.hpp the return type size_t, as d08686b has it. The headers of f331cd1+half-tables passed the test programs output, media_type, escape, room and troff of f331cd1 (linked with gtest_main) with clang++-23 -std=c++23 and g++-16 -std=c++26 -freflection, -O2 -march=x86-64-v3 -Wall -Wextra -Werror, before this run; the other patched states passed them before the run of table-size-20261114T091231Z.json; include/ of the repository is not changed",
 "probe": {"commit": "244fa260812abef7cb38e2d5ea277566b1c5e444", "files": ["bench/probes/table-size/probe.cpp", "bench/probes/table-size/run.sh", "bench/probes/table-size/inside.sh", "bench/probes/table-size/class-tables.patch", "bench/probes/table-size/class-fields.patch", "bench/probes/table-size/half-tables.patch"], "dirty_files": 1, "dirty_files_are": "bench/results/scalar-writers-20261114T093506Z.json, the result of an invalid run, not committed and deleted since; no file of the probe"},
